****
My NAO ascension streak now stands at 5 games.  I'm also 9 for my last
13.

Before I get to the details on this game, I'd like to share some
logfile weirdness.  All 5 games from my current streak have scores of
1.8x million points.  Talk about consistent!

The first half of this game went by in a flash.  I was in "the zone".
I managed to go from start to quest completion in one session.  The
details are a bit hazy.

I entered the dungeon intent on doing some shopping.  I was a tourist,
after all!  Before I reached the first shop, I stumbled across some +0
gauntlets of power.   The first shop I came to was a bookstore.  I was
rather surprised to find an amicable shopkeeper willing to give me a
break on his pricing (18 Charisma will do that!).

On Dlvl.05, an abandoned icebox had lots of yummy treats.  The
shrieker corpse left me feeling healthy.  Just below that, sauvaigne's
ghost was hovering over a pile of loot.  "CSI: Yendor" indicated this
was a monk bones pile.  The robe in the pile, and the scimitars
scattered about both proved very useful.

The entrance to sokoban was Dlvl:09.  I made a mistake on the 2nd
level of sokoban.  Fortunately I had a wand of teleportation.  I spent
two zaps fixing the problem without trashing my luck.  The top level
had a bag of holding and a peaceful co-aligned unicorn.

While rounding the corner a werewolf summoned help.  I was worried,
since he brought in 3 winter wolves.  I teleported one away and dealt
with the other two from a "safe" spot near the corner where they
couldn't breathe frost.  I picked up cold resistance from one of them.

After leaving Sokoban and while on my way to the mines, I took a
trapdoor down to Dlvl.11.  After a close call with second a werewolf,
I made my way up.

Just above minetown, I picked up a magic lamp.  Izchak had another.
After price-identifying a bunch of stuff, it was time to make holy
water.  The minetown priest was cross-aligned, so I had to trek out of
the mines to an altar higher up to make holy water and get MR +
reflection.

At T:10763, the first lamp wish was used on the blessed Eyes of the
Overworld.  Conventional wisdom says "wfte!" [1] if you're neutral,
but the combination of astral vision and invokable enlightenment is
absurdly powerful in it's own right.  Next up was some blessed greased
+2 silver dragon scale mail (I got +0).

In between leaving the mines and reaching the quest, I maximized my
luck (unicorn, sokoban top level) and got crowned (Hello Vorpy!)

Mines end was the catacombs, which worked out well for a change.  I
left the mines for good shortly before T:15000 and started to make my
way to the castle.  Quite rare for me, I did the quest before the
castle.  I had MR, reflection, and was XL:14 thanks to the home-level
wraiths.

I slept the Master of Thieves before wailing away.  I managed to kill
him before he woke up.  But wait ... he had an amulet of life saving.
I had to sleep him and kill him a second time.  The first session
ended with me standing near the quest portal, about to leave (and
burdened thanks to all the not-yet sorted loot).

After a brief stop-off at sokoban to drop off excess junk, I made my
way to the Castle.  I arrived at T:22198 to be greeted by a arch
lich.  He dropped an athame.  The drawbridge dance took care of the
outer courtyard

I did my usual trick of teleporting to the Vibrating Square then
mapping Gehennom backwards.  Shortly before arriving at Orcustown, a
chickatrice dropped a corpse.  This made some nice statues.  Orcus'
statue had not one but *two* wands of death.  He's such a nice host!
Baalzebub and Asmodeus were given their usual bribes (less than 10gp,
each).  Juiblex was killed without me stepping off the downstair.

When I returned to the Castle after scouting Gehennom, I had 141 MaxHP
and very little alchemy fodder.  A very inefficient alchemy session
netted 2 potions of full healing (1x!speed, 2x!healing, 1x!gain
energy, and 2x!holy water).  That and 2 potions of gain level got me
up to 165.  Still not in my comfort zone, but better.

The ascension run was mostly uneventful, despite rodney showing up a
boatload of times.  The "grab the goods and go" phase took a 1,178
turns.  I was somehow faster than my recent 1,244 turn "warpspeed
climb".  Go figure.

Astral wasn't too bad.  I arrived on the left.  Death was left.  To
paraphrase rax "LET'S ROLL!"  After clearing his courtyard, I found
myself surrounded at less than 1/2 HP.  Time to use a b!full healing
(I keep 4 on hand for the run, rarely do I use one).  I had to kill
Death on the way out (+6 darts are nice).  Then, I stupidly zapped /
tele in her corpse's direction.  OOPS!  Creative jumping got me out of
that one.

The center altar was guarded by Famine.  Careful maneuvering got me to
the neutral altar at HP:173(173).

For anyone interested, the ttyrec of the ascension run can be found
via one of these two links:
http://alt.org/nethack/ttyrec/cdi/2007-05-15.22:37:00.ttyrec
http://alt.org/nethack/ttyrec/cdi/2007-05-15.22:37:00.ttyrec.bz2

I hope this game was as entertaining/educational as the "warpspeed
climb"

-cdi

